    "content": "Starting in December 2026, the Selective Service System will automatically register eligible men (citizens and residents aged 18–25) for the military draft using existing federal data. This change, part of the fiscal 2026 National Defense Authorization Act, removes the need for individual self-registration, aiming to improve compliance and streamline the process.Key Details About Automatic Registration:What is Changing: The responsibility shifts from individuals to the Selective Service System, which will pull data from other federal agencies.Who is Affected: Almost all male U.S. citizens and male immigrants residing in the U.S. between 18 and 25 years old.Is a Draft Starting? No. This is not a reinstatement of the draft, which requires congressional and presidential authorization.Why It's Occurring: The change aims to ensure compliance, as registration is still mandatory by law, and to update records without requiring manual sign-ups.Penalties: Failure to be registered (even if automatic fails) can still result in the loss of federal student loans, jobs, and citizenship opportunities.The initiative aims to improve accuracy in the potential military draft database, which has seen declining registration rates, while ensuring that all eligible individuals are prepared for a national crisis.",
